  "description": "The application **my-app** will run under the user **appuser** with three instances, each allocated **0.5\u202fCPU**, **256\u202fMiB of memory**, and **0\u202fGiB of disk**. It will be launched in a Docker container using the image **nginx:latest**, set to the **BRIDGE** network, with **forcePullImage** enabled and **privileged** mode disabled. No extra Docker parameters or host\u2011volume mounts are defined. The container exposes **port\u202f8080** internally, which is mapped to a dynamically assigned host port and advertised externally as **service port\u202f9000** over **TCP**. The command line arguments passed to the process are `--port 8080`. Environment variables are set to **ENVIRONMENT=production** and **LOG_LEVEL=info**. The service accepts any resource role (`*`), has no placement constraints, and declares a dependency on `../service`.\n\nHealth checking is performed with the command `curl -f http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1`. The check uses the **HTTP** protocol on **port index\u202f0**, targeting the path **/health**. It allows a **30\u2011second grace period**, runs every **10\u202fseconds**, times out after **5\u202fseconds**, and tolerates up to **3 consecutive failures**; HTTP\u202f1xx responses are not ignored. Labels identify the service as belonging to **team=backend** and **project=my-app**, and the advertised port list contains **9000**. The application does not require a specific host port (`requirePorts: false`) and will be fetched from the URI **http://example.com/app.tar.gz**, with an associated store URL **https://store.example.com/app**.\n\nThe upgrade strategy reserves a **minimum health capacity of 0.5** and permits a **maximum over\u2011capacity of 0.2**. Restart back\u2011off starts at **10\u202fseconds**, grows by a factor of **1.5**, and is capped at a **maximum launch delay of 3600\u202fseconds**. The configuration is versioned at **2023\u201108\u201101T12:00:00Z**.",
  "reference_json": {
    "id": "my-app",
    "cpus": 0.5,
    "mem": 256,
    "disk": 0,
    "instances": 3,
    "args": [
      "--port",
      "8080"
    ],
    "container": {
      "type": "DOCKER",
      "docker": {
        "image": "nginx:latest",
        "network": "BRIDGE",
        "forcePullImage": true,
        "privileged": false,
        "parameters": [],
        "portMappings": [
          {
            "containerPort": 8080,
            "hostPort": 0,
            "servicePort": 9000,
            "protocol": "tcp"
          }
        ]
      },
      "volumes": []
    },
    "env": {
      "ENVIRONMENT": "production",
      "LOG_LEVEL": "info"
    },
    "acceptedResourceRoles": [
      "*"
    ],
    "constraints": {},
    "healthChecks": [
      {
        "command": "curl -f http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1",
        "gracePeriodSeconds": 30,
        "intervalSeconds": 10,
        "timeoutSeconds": 5,
        "maxConsecutiveFailures": 3,
        "protocol": "HTTP",
        "portIndex": 0,
        "path": "/health",
        "ignoreHttp1xx": false
      }
    ],
    "labels": {
      "team": "backend",
      "project": "my-app"
    },
    "ports": [
      9000
    ],
    "requirePorts": false,
    "uris": [
      "http://example.com/app.tar.gz"
    ],
    "storeUrls": [
      "https://store.example.com/app"
    ],
    "upgradeStrategy": {
      "minimumHealthCapacity": 0.5,
      "maximumOverCapacity": 0.2
    },
    "backoffSeconds": 10,
    "backoffFactor": 1.5,
    "maxLaunchDelaySeconds": 3600,
    "dependencies": [
      "../service"
    ],
    "version": "2023-08-01T12:00:00Z",
    "user": "appuser"
  }
